  "title": "Red Hat Security Advisory: thunderbird security update",
  "description": "Multiple security vulnerabilities have been identified and addressed in Mozilla Thunderbird, a standalone mail and newsgroup client. These include numerous use-after-free bugs, sandbox escapes, privilege escalations, information disclosures, spoofing issues, and boundary condition errors across various components such as JavaScript GC, DOM, Graphics, Audio/Video, Networking, and Security. Additionally, a vulnerability allowing NTLM credential leakage on Windows via feed subscriptions has been fixed. Red Hat has released an important security update for Thunderbird in Red Hat Enterprise Linux 9.8 Extended Update Support to address these issues.",
